Copyright (c) 2026 VibePier contributors

VibePier derives from vibed, the open-source Ulanzi Vibe Key driver by
Ben Gittins: https://github.com/ihavespoons/vibed

The original MIT copyright notice is preserved in LICENSE. The new repository
starts with a consolidated release commit; this does not change the original
code's license or authorship. Further work includes the Mac menu app, Android
companion, AI session integrations, voice controls, and self-hosted relay.

VibePier is an independent community project. It is not affiliated with
Ulanzi, OpenAI, Anthropic, or the makers of ZCode. Referenced product names and
logos belong to their respective owners. BlackHole is an optional external
audio driver and is not included in the installation packages.

Original VibePier brand vectors and source-controlled illustrations are
distributed under the repository's MIT license. The README scene illustrations
and editorial covers were created with AI image generation; they are conceptual
artwork, not screenshots or evidence of product behavior. Generation records
for the covers are in assets/GENERATION-PROMPTS.md.
